id: TASK_028_V006
title: Document in-memory task queue limitation and plan Redis/RQ migration path
status: REJECTED
priority: medium
depends_on: []

rejection_reason: >
  Task scope creep beyond documentation. The task is labeled as documentation but includes
  code changes (adding module-level warnings, configuration flags) that require monitoring
  infrastructure and architecture review. This is partial implementation disguised as documentation.

required_fixes:
  - Option 1: Split into pure documentation task - only create TASK_QUEUE_MIGRATION.md
  - Option 2: Expand into full Redis/RQ integration plan with proper architecture review
  - Remove runtime warning/code change goals from documentation task

original_description: >
  The TaskQueue uses asyncio.Queue — an in-memory queue. All queued tasks are lost on
  application restart. This is an MVP limitation that needs documentation and a migration plan.

goals:
  - Document the current in-memory queue limitation
  - Add a comment/warning in the code about task loss on restart  # CODE CHANGE - NOT DOCUMENTATION
  - Create a migration plan for Redis/RQ integration
  - Add a configuration flag to warn in production  # CODE CHANGE - NOT DOCUMENTATION

files:
  - path: src/mkobi/core/task_queue.py
    targets:
      - type: class
        name: TaskQueue
  - path: docs/TASK_QUEUE_MIGRATION.md
    targets:
      - type: new_file
        description: "Migration plan document"

notes: >
  REJECTED: Scope creep - task includes code changes not appropriate for documentation task.
  See rejection_reason for required fixes.